<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9335"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 8:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Did I hear that correctly? What crimes would only have a 2 year s.o.l.? <BR> <BR>Better question, what do they suspect him of that they cannot charge him with?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9335-->
<!--Post: 9353--><!--Time: 1109482844-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9353"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 9:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Capital murder in Kansas has no statute of limitations. I don&#39;t know if it will affect the aggravated circumstances or not. i.e. Sometimes, If a state would say count murder in the act of a felony as a capital crime, and home invasion was a felony, the statute of limitations could run out on the home invasion and a defense lawyer could argue for a reduced charge on the killing. <BR> <BR>But BTK will not be walking free anymore in this lifetime. ever. no chance. never happen.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9353-->
<!--Post: 9355--><!--Time: 1109483322-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9355"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 9:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Keep a suicide watch on his cell! I don&#39;t recall the man&#39;s name but a Missouri serial killer hanged himself, rapidly, and it was an extra dose of pain for the family of each victim. Highly unlikely with the spotlight now burning so brightly but you never know.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9355-->
<!--Post: 9373--><!--Time: 1109485934-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9373"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 26, 2005 - 10:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Its not unusual for serial murderers to commit suicide. Johann Unterweger, an Austrian serial murderer who murdered prostitutes in Austria, Czechoslovakia and California during the early 1990s committed suicide. He waited until the verdict was delivered. Committing suicide is the final attempt for a psychopath to exert control. The psychopath would rather die at their own hand than be punished by the judiciary.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9373-->
<!--Post: 9437--><!--Time: 1109526257-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9437"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 9:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->BtK cant be charged with capitol murder. And he still has to be convicted. I hope it is him, but justice can be odd at times.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9437-->
<!--Post: 10717--><!--Time: 1110146700-->
